-- | AccessControl capability contracts — the substrate of the whole admin layer.
--
-- A `RoleCapability` is a bearer credential, co-signed by the registry
-- administrator, that grants one `Role` to one `assignee`, optionally scoped to
-- a single instrument. Possession of a valid capability *is* the authorization:
-- a gated choice fetches the capability the caller presents and asserts it is
-- admin-signed, names the caller, carries the required role, and is in scope.
-- This replaces EVM's runtime role-map lookups with a cryptographic signatory
-- check (docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §3).
--
-- Ownable and Pausable are not separate mechanisms: the `Admin` role is the
-- owner / `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE`, and pause is gated on a `Pauser` capability.
--
-- Keyless by necessity — Daml LF 2.1 dropped contract keys. Capabilities are
-- referenced by `ContractId`, delivered to gated choices through the existing
-- `ChoiceContext` plumbing (`ContextUtils.roleCapabilityContextKey`) or as an
-- explicit choice argument.
module SimpleToken.Admin.Capability where

import Splice.Api.Token.HoldingV1 (InstrumentId)

import SimpleToken.Admin.Errors
import SimpleToken.Admin.Roles (Role)

-- | A capability granting `assignee` a single `role` over the registry governed
-- by `admin`, optionally narrowed to one instrument via `scope`.
--
-- `admin` is the immutable registry root party (the instrument issuer). Every
-- instrument on a `SimpleTokenRules` shares that admin, so a `scope = None`
-- capability is registry-wide; `scope = Some iid` is least-privilege, valid only
-- for that instrument. Operational "ownership" is the `Admin` role; handing it
-- to a new governance party (and revoking the old) is the ownership-transfer
-- analogue — no party reassignment, no rebind. See docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §5.
template RoleCapability
  with
    admin : Party                   -- ^ The registry root party that issued this capability.
    assignee : Party                -- ^ The party granted the role.
    role : Role                     -- ^ The single role granted.
    scope : Optional InstrumentId   -- ^ None = registry-wide; Some = limited to that instrument.
  where
    -- INV-31: only the registry root (or its delegate, via TokenAdministrator)
    -- can mint a capability; it is admin-signed and therefore unforgeable.
    signatory admin
    -- The assignee can see (and present) their own capability, nothing more.
    observer assignee

-- | Does a capability's scope authorize an operation requiring `requiredScope`?
--
-- A registry-wide capability (`None`) authorizes any operation. An
-- instrument-scoped capability authorizes only operations on that exact
-- instrument — in particular it does NOT authorize registry-wide operations
-- (e.g. pausing the whole registry), preserving least privilege.
scopeAuthorizes : Optional InstrumentId -> Optional InstrumentId -> Bool
scopeAuthorizes capScope requiredScope = case capScope of
  None -> True
  Some s -> requiredScope == Some s

-- | Assert that `caller` holds `role` for the registry governed by
-- `expectedAdmin`, in scope for `requiredScope`. Fetches the presented
-- capability and validates it.
--
-- `requiredScope = None` denotes a registry-wide operation (e.g. pause, role
-- management); `requiredScope = Some iid` denotes an operation on instrument
-- `iid` (e.g. minting that instrument).
--
-- # Invariants enforced:
-- - INV-27: capability admin must equal the registry admin
-- - INV-28: capability assignee must equal the caller (anti-impersonation)
-- - INV-29: capability role must equal the required role
-- - INV-30: capability scope must authorize the operation's scope
--
-- Soundness without keys: the capability is admin-signed (unforgeable) and
-- names a specific assignee, so the worst an adversary can do is present a
-- capability they do not hold and fail their own authorization.
requireRole : Party -> Role -> Party -> Optional InstrumentId -> ContractId RoleCapability -> Update ()
requireRole caller role expectedAdmin requiredScope capCid = do
  cap <- fetch capCid
  assertMsg eCapabilityAdminMismatch (cap.admin == expectedAdmin)
  assertMsg eCapabilityAssigneeMismatch (cap.assignee == caller)
  assertMsg eCapabilityRoleMismatch (cap.role == role)
  assertMsg eCapabilityScopeMismatch (scopeAuthorizes cap.scope requiredScope)
